{"title":"Regular Octahedron","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definition\">Definition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Regular_Octahedron&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Definition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <b>regular octahedron</b> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Platonic_solid\" title=\"Platonic solid\">Platonic solid</a> that has 8 faces. It is also a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Regular_Polytope\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Regular Polytope\">regular</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Octahedron\" title=\"Octahedron\">octahedron</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"AMC_10_example\">AMC 10 example</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Regular_Octahedron&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: AMC 10 example\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">2006 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24</a>\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Regular_Octahedron&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018105044\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.013 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 14/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 295/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/50000